nio: mark the steps inside bsdinit_task

Run 606 confirms the init thread now reaches bsdinit_task through bsd_ast
("defer bsdinit_task to init thread AST" is on the panel), and the earlier
fatal is gone.  But "CHK before load_init" never appears, so bsdinit_task
is stuck before load_init_program().  The swapfile messages are from an
unrelated background thread, not this path.

Put panel marks around process_name(), ux_handler_setup() and
vm_init_before_launchd() so the next photograph names the exact call that
does not return.  Diagnosis only, no behaviour change.

diff --git a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
index c4bb930..8d62245 100644
--- a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
@@ -1310,18 +1310,25 @@ native_owner_root_checkpoint(int apple, int owner, dev_t device)
 void
 bsdinit_task(void)
 {
+	nio_bmark("\nnio: BT enter");
 	proc_t p = current_proc();
 
 	process_name("init", p);
 
+	nio_bmark("\nnio: BT pre-ux_handler");
 	/* Set up exception-to-signal reflection */
 	ux_handler_setup();
+	nio_bmark("\nnio: BT post-ux_handler");
+
 
 #if CONFIG_MACF
 	mac_cred_label_associate_user(proc_ucred(p));
 #endif
 
+	nio_bmark("\nnio: BT pre-vm_init");
 	vm_init_before_launchd();
+	nio_bmark("\nnio: BT post-vm_init");
+
 
 #if CONFIG_XNUPOST
 	int result = bsd_list_tests();
